Median of Two Sorted Arrays

Problem: LeetCode 4

Difficulty: Hard

Approach: Merge Two Sorted Arrays

1. Create a new array to store elements from both arrays.
2. Use three pointers: "i", "j", and "k".
3. Compare elements from both arrays.
4. Insert the smaller element into the new array.
5. Copy any remaining elements.
6. Find the median using the total number of elements.

Median Formula

- Odd number of elements: Return the middle element.
- Even number of elements: Calculate the average of the two middle elements.
 solution -
class Solution {
    public double findMedianSortedArrays(int[] nums1, int[] nums2) {

        int[] arr = new int[nums1.length + nums2.length];

        int i = 0, j = 0, k = 0;

        while (i < nums1.length && j < nums2.length) {

            if (nums1[i] < nums2[j]) {
                arr[k++] = nums1[i++];
            } else {
                arr[k++] = nums2[j++];
            }
        }

        while (i < nums1.length) {
            arr[k++] = nums1[i++];
        }

        while (j < nums2.length) {
            arr[k++] = nums2[j++];
        }

        int n = arr.length;

        if (n % 2 == 1) {
            return arr[n / 2];
        } else {
            return (arr[n / 2 - 1] + arr[n / 2]) / 2.0;
        }
    }
}

Complexity Analysis

- Time Complexity: O(m + n)
- Space Complexity: O(m + n)

Note: This is a basic merging approach. The problem's required optimal solution uses binary search with O(log(min(m,n))) time complexity.

Key Learning
This problem helps us understand:
- Two-pointer technique
- Merging sorted arrays
- Finding the median
- Binary search (in the optimal approach)
